#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Noise example 1: Basic bit-flip error noise model {#noise-example-1-basic-"
"bit-flip-error-noise-model}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's consider a simple toy noise model example common in quantum "
"information theory research:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When applying a single-qubit gate, flip the state of the qubit with "
"probability `p_gate1`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When applying a two-qubit gate, apply single-qubit errors to each qubit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When resetting a qubit, reset to 1 instead of 0 with probability "
"`p_reset`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When measuring a qubit, flip the state of the qubit with probability "
"`p_meas`.\n"
msgstr ""

